------------------
ChuMP VERSIONS log
------------------
0.0.4
=====
Infinite chump

(added) chump now supports dependencies!
    * chump packages can now depend on other packages and chucmp will automatically select
      the best version, download all dependencies, and tell you if a package combination is
      not possible
(added) Chumpinate (now v0.2.0) can now addDependency(...) to add package dependencies in chump
     * ver.addPackageDependency("Rec", "1.0.0", "2.0.0"); // add Rec as a dep and restrict versions
     * ver.addPackageDependency("Rec"); // add Rec as a dependency with no version restrictions
(added) Chumpinate Package.version() will output version string of Chumpinate package (now v0.2.0)
(improved) Chumpinate PackageVersion methods will now throw exceptions in chuck-land for methods that could already throw
	   exceptions, but were not percolated up into chuck
	
(improved) made chump cli output formatting more consistent

(improved) added OS architecture and ChucK version to info messages
	   when a package isn't available on the specific system configuration

0.0.3
=====
20,000 chumps under the sea

(added) chump doc command
    * 'chump doc <package>' to open a documentation web page for <package> (if it exists)
(added) chump examples command
    * 'chump examples <package>' to open the examples directory for <package> (if it exists)
(added) chump list -u/--updates
    * lists only packages that have an update available on your system
(fixed) shorter connection timeout when downloading manifest
    * chump attempts to update the package manifest on startup. previously this would
      use the default 300s connction timeout meaning that if connection to the
      ccrma server was slow/flaky chump would stall. This timeout has been lowered to
      three seconds.

